## How to find something

### 1. By global line number

```powershell
$line = 1234567
Import-Csv .\INDEX.csv |
    Where-Object { [int]$_.StartLine -le $line -and [int]$_.EndLine -ge $line } |
    Select-Object Part, FileName, StartLine, EndLine
```

Open the named chunk and jump to `line - StartLine + 1` inside it.

### 2. By substring search (text grep across all chunks)

```powershell
# PowerShell
Select-String -Path '.\{{BASE_NAME}}_part_*.txt' -Pattern '<your-pattern>' -SimpleMatch |
    Select-Object Path, LineNumber, Line
```

```bash
# Git Bash / WSL
grep -nH '<your-pattern>' {{BASE_NAME}}_part_*.txt
```

The reported `LineNumber` is **local to the chunk**. Convert to a global line
number: `global = StartLine_of_that_chunk + LocalLine - 1`.

### 3. By byte offset

`StartByte` / `EndByte` in `INDEX.csv` let you reconstruct any byte range of the
original from a contiguous run of chunks without ever materializing the full file.

