## Reconstructing the original (sanity check)

```powershell
$chunks = Get-ChildItem .\{{BASE_NAME}}_part_*.txt | Sort-Object Name
$out    = [System.IO.File]::Create('.\_rebuilt.tmp')
foreach ($c in $chunks) {
    $bytes = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($c.FullName)
    $out.Write($bytes, 0, $bytes.Length)
}
$out.Dispose()

(Get-FileHash '<path-to-original>\{{SOURCE_FILENAME}}' -Algorithm SHA256).Hash
(Get-FileHash '.\_rebuilt.tmp'                          -Algorithm SHA256).Hash
# The two hashes MUST match exactly.
Remove-Item .\_rebuilt.tmp
```

```bash
# bash equivalent
cat $(ls {{BASE_NAME}}_part_*.txt | sort) > _rebuilt.tmp
sha256sum '<path-to-original>/{{SOURCE_FILENAME}}' _rebuilt.tmp
rm _rebuilt.tmp
```

